WEBVTT

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.980
Huh?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.740
What should I do?

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.540
Why?

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.360
I...

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.480
...made Kazama cry.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.210
All right, we'll have another strategy meeting at your house today.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.100
We'll be studying for the test.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.760
We'll see you out front!

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.330
Don't be late, either!

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.490
That's my line.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.170
I wonder what I have for a snack today?

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.490
Hey, Murasame-san.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:27.100
You seem to be getting along well
with those two lately.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.420
Hachisuka and Taema?

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.200
Yeah, so...

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.180
Are they...

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.510
...really going out?!

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.020
We actually asked!

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.700
Well... I wonder about that.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.270
Shouldn't you ask them directly when it comes to something like this?

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:54.920
We're classmates, so there's no need to be shy.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.880
Didn't you two head home already?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.380
We came back when we heard our names mentioned.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.340
We'll ask you directly, then.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.790
You two are going out, right?

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.040
You're always together.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.790
You have a suspicious air about you.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.540
Even though some of the boys
are interested in you...

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.790
...we find it hard to believe otherwise.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.300
There's no way you two aren't going out!

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.440
That said, just what do you
do together as girls?!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:30.310
While I have no obligation to explain myself in order to satisfy the idle curiosity of others...

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.560
...does the gender of an individual
factor into whom you love?

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.200
Yeah.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.570
It does.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.320
In other words,

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.570
you two are going out!

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.050
Yuri? For real?

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.300
Ah, no...

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.220
Anyway, it's a matter of preference—

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.580
Give it a rest already!

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:55.080
That's not something to discuss
openly in the classroom!

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.850
Why are you being such a spoilsport, Aoi?

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.900
I expected more of you, Murasame-san!

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.090
What, me?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.080
You're the class president,
so you shouldn't...

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.570
...well...

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.100
...be talking about such shameless things!

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.350
But I wasn't.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.400
To call other people "shameless" — how unpleasant.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:16.860
What are you...

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.320
Are you trying to intimidate me?

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.250
That's my Tomoe-chan!

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.570
You calmly do what others dare not!

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.120
That's what I love about you!

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.750
Rather, you should be upset.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:51.020
Well? That's what you call shameless—

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.360
Aoi-san...

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.900
Young ones these days are all talk.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.650
You're the same age, though.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.460
Ah, I guess I never told you.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.160
Tomoe-chan took two years off from school,
so she turns 18 this year.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.840
Wh-Why haven't you told us before?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.870
You never asked.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.700
Sumi-chan, shouldn't we go after Aoi-san?

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.230
I've been defiled.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.820
Please forgive me, Masaka-oneesama!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.080
Azusa, a loveless kiss means nothing.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.420
Think of it as being bitten by a dog,
and forget about it.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.800
That's right!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.590
What matters are the feelings
we have for each other.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.430
Yes! Just as you hold me in your heart...

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.430
As long as you have that,
you can never be tainted!

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:19.440
Truly, Masaka-oneesama is the only one for me!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:34.450
Orino Masaka-san, is it?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.420
She's not quite that well known yet.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.040
But she's truly amazing!

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:46.220
She writes about the friendship
between girls in an old style.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.470
Little information about her has been made public,

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.970
but I'm sure she's both beautiful and romantic!

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.770
You're... probably right.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.840
I'm sorry, Aoi-san.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:06.480
Orino Masaka is the pen name Kazama's brother writes under.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.990
The work is a reflection of the author!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.490
That's why I embrace Masaka-oneesama and love this world so!

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:20.080
I couldn't possibly tell her the truth.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.290
"And so, she let but a single
sigh escape her alluring lips."

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.880
"No, it may have been a single stanza."

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.390
Oh, that's from the short story that won her the rookie of the year award.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.100
You seem to know her well;
that hasn't even been printed yet.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.050
Still, isn't it just riveting?

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.900
You know about it, Murasame-san!

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.900
Quite in depth, too!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.890
Well, I guess...

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.410
Not good; I'm getting sucked in.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.870
What a relief.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:01.320
There aren't any other fans in the area,
so I was worried that she wasn't very popular.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:09.690
If you're a fan of hers, you know that people as brazen as Hachisuka-san are mistaken.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:14.760
Well, yeah... Certainly, it's a little...

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:15.680
I knew it!

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.960
We have similar interests.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:25.210
Love between girls should be more... secretive.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.190
Enduring, like pure water.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.690
That's why I find it beautiful.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.070
For example, a place like this.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.950
After school, in the corner of the building,

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:43.560
the distant voices of the students
sound like the ocean waves

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.960
and soon fade away in the gentle breeze.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:55.720
There, in that place, there are only the two of them gazing at each other.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.600
Out!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.350
I'm so sorry! I was out of line!

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.640
No, don't worry about it.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:12.110
I'm glad that I found
someone who understands me.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.000
I'm sure we'll become good friends.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.120
You're right.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.210
You'll have to forgive Hachisuka for what she did.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.920
She's not really a bad person.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.000
It's all right.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.570
I feel much better thanks to you, Murasame-san.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.550
Let's go back to the classroom.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.630
Y-Yeah.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.060
Sumi-chan?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.650
K-Kazama?

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:58.900
This is... well...

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.280
Ah, Kazama!

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.880
I'm sorry, Aoi-san!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.050
Kazama!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.460
Hold on!

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:10.960
That was...

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:13.960
Kazama?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.520
I understand.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.470
You just slipped and fell, right?

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:27.600
Right! That's what happened, so...

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.060
Huh?

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.860
Oh no. Why am I...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.640
Kazama...

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:48.870
Murasame-san!

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:52.290
Geez, where did you run off to?

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.630
They're arguing back in the classroom,
and it's got bad.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.300
You're the class president,
so do something about it!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:58.880
Hold it...

00:10:59.180 --> 00:10:59.760
Not now—

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:00.960
What's the matter?
Not now—

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:01.300
What's the matter?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:01.930
Hold on a second...

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:03.390
Look, we have to hurry!

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.350
What about Akemiya-kun?

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:06.540
Who's that?

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.170
What should I do?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.650
I...

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:19.140
...made Kazama cry.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.700
We got into an argument
over what to call her.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:27.450
Which one seems good to you, Murasame-san?

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.780
Hachi!

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:33.960
Well, I don't mind that.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:41.470
You mustn't, Murasame-san!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.680
But... why?

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.420
Why did Kazama cry?

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.490
Because of me...

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:14.120
Why would she...

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.340
Oh my. Please, do come in.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:17.340
Excuse me.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.090
Good afternoon!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.130
Afternoon!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:33.390
Now, I'd like to begin the 12th Girls' Club Establishment Meeting, but...

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.110
Aren't we going to study for the test?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.150
We'll do that after the meeting.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.900
However, before that...

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.700
Did something happen?

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.910
Beats me.

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:51.160
Hello, Ushio-chan?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:55.920
I don't get it!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.420
Why was she crying back there?!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.300
What happened?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.220
Beats me.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.180
Oh my. How lively.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.530
Kazama-kun, Murasame-kun.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.830
I'm sorry; my hands slipped.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.840
Just what do you think you're doing?!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.420
Just because you're older—

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:48.080
I don't know what happened,
but don't you two need some time to talk about it alone?

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.090
What is it?

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.700
It's not just due to being two years older, is it?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.860
I wonder if my shirt will dry
before I need to go home.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:10.870
I'm sorry, but our dryer is broken.

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.790
There's one in the dojo for the gi, though.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.370
It's sunny today,
so we can dry them anywhere.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.380
Yeah, that's true.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:33.470
What were those tears before, then?!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.890
I just don't understand girls!

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:37.890
You can't do that, Sumi-chan!

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:41.400
You'll tear the shirt if
you wash it that furiously.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.900
You really aren't very good
at these things, Sumi-chan.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:50.540
You're a diligent student,
good at sports, and excel at karate.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:53.010
You're almost like a boy.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.410
That's it!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.160
That must be why I cried before!

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:04.710
The Sumi-chan who assaulted Aoi-san seemed just like a violent man!

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:06.630
A violent... man?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.300
The worst kind of people!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.930
They use their strength to do
whatever they want to women!

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.560
Ah, what a relief. That's that!

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.920
I've been in constant haze until now.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.940
A violent... man?

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.940
You wouldn't, would you?

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.950
Sumi-chan, you wouldn't do something
like that, would you?

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.960
I wouldn't do that to anyone...

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.490
...but you.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.840
I'm sorry!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.850
I spilled it too!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.610
It couldn't be.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:12.850
For a brief moment,
it seemed as if she was waiting for me to say it.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.460
Or not...

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:20.770
Even so, dare I hope...

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:30.580
...that within her heart,
Kazama harbors feelings for me?

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:36.010
It's really hot today as well.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:40.390
They might dry faster out here than in the dryer.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.020
You may be right.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:46.440
Anyway, what were you
talking to Aoi-san about?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.190
Ah, about that—

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.020
Hey!
Ah, about that—

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.280
Murasame-san!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:54.570
Look, look! I'm making these!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:58.660
The Orino Masaka fan club circular!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.040
Orino... Masaka?

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:05.040
It couldn't be...

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.840
Wh-Why are you two here?!

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.050
It's because we're friends.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:18.660
I see. A fanzine for girl novels, huh?

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:24.350
However, looking through this,
it seems like you're the sole author.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.560
Let me see.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:30.570
May I... go home?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.440
"Every sentence expresses Onee-sama's dreams..."

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.070
Please don't...

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:36.110
Isn't it nice when it's so lively?

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.070
Isn't it just.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.710
I see.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:47.580
See what?

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:51.040
I don't care much for the narcissism,

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:55.590
but I can tell how devoted you are to the author by the way you write.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.090
It really is quite passionate.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.600
Please forgive me for my churlish actions earlier.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.850
You have potential.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.130
We need you.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.250
Won't you join the Girls' Club?

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.110
If you like girls,
you must join the Girls' Club.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:16.360
I-I don't really have... that kind of preference.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:22.080
I only love the untainted world
spun by Masaka-oneesama!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.250
Don't mistake me for one of your
crass and impure kind!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.200
Don't you agree, Murasame-san?!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.880
Ah, how should I put it...

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:36.670
Are... you... an... idiot?

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:40.390
Your pertinacious ramblings
are just annoying, Big Brow.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:42.170
Big Brow?

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:47.520
You've tried to recruit me once before!

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.980
Have we now?

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.160
Beats me.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.520
Ah, it's already four.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.530
I guess it's about time we
started studying for the test.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:58.030
Yeah, I suppose.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.360
Ah, what a bore.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.530
I'll be heading home, then.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:10.010
Ah, I see. I'm sorry that I
couldn't be more hospitable.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:14.040
Not at all; it's my fault for
showing up unannounced.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.670
I'll leave these books with you,

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:20.260
so if you don't mind, would you read them and tell me your thoughts?

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.820
Sure. Thank you.

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:58.980
Excuse me, but what would
you girls like for dinner?

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:01.340
I'm starving!

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.760
Oh, it's already this late.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.340
Meat! I want to have meat!

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.140
Me too!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.810
You two have no shame.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.060
Aren't you being a little domineering about what you want to eat?

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.970
Oh, well.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.480
I'll make sure to return your clothes.

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.290
Ah, don't worry about it.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:20.920
Are you really going home?

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.490
I have to make dinner for my brother.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.200
Really, Sumi-chan.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.660
I can come over at any time.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.500
Ah, take this.

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:36.640
Your brother might want to read it.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.710
But...

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:42.520
Aoi-san left quite a few of them.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.690
You can return it once he's read it.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.140
Thank you.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.720
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.330
Tomorrow.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.780
Well, then.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.100
Take care.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.240
Um...

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.580
Geez, Sumi-chan. I won't get home at this rate.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.750
S-Sorry.

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:17.390
Bye bye.

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:06.420
I know her!

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:09.040
She sent this to the editorial department too.

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:10.860
Oh, is that so?

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:14.240
So you go to the same school?

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:18.870
I have to be careful not to reveal
that you're Orino Masaka.

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:23.000
So you say, but it's not like I'm actually well known.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.130
Indeed, you really aren't.

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:32.140
I'll work harder. Yeah.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.560
That's not what I meant...

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.390
Yeah...

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:43.200
It's all right.

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:52.410
It's all right!
